# Mandatory setup.sh
RULE: Every repo MUST have scripts/setup.sh copied from the canonical SSOT template. No repo may define its own ad-hoc setup flow.
SSOT: unified-trading-pm/scripts/setup.sh
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/setup-standards.md
KEY PROPERTIES:
  - Idempotent — safe to re-run at any time without side effects.
  - Skips completed steps — the .setup-stamp file tracks when deps were last installed; setup.sh skips reinstall if the stamp is current.
  - No interactive prompts — must run unattended in CI and locally.
  - CI-aware — detects CI environments and adjusts behavior accordingly.
FORBIDDEN:
  - `pip install` — always use `uv`.
  - Manual venv creation outside setup.sh.
  - Interactive `read` prompts or any user input.
  - `os.getenv()` fallbacks in setup logic — use UnifiedCloudConfig.
RELATIONSHIP: quality-gates.sh and quickmerge.sh may source setup.sh for bootstrap. setup.sh is the single owner of environment preparation — no other script may duplicate its responsibilities.
